    AI4DEV-62: the single-seat organisation and the single-developer project
    
    Slice 2 of two - the partner item's own slice, riding this branch. Both invariants land as
    SHAPE rather than as a rule some writer applies, because there is no writer to apply one: no
    invite path and no attach path exists in this tree.
    
    What lands:
    
    * migration 20260811130000 - a unique index on org_memberships (org_id) alone, which is
      strictly stronger than the composite primary key and leaves no room for a second membership
      row in an organisation; public.projects, whose single nullable assigned_volunteer_id makes a
      collaborator seat unrepresentable; a BEFORE UPDATE guard that refuses re-pointing an occupied
      seat at a different account; row-level security on, and an explicit revoke all from anon,
      authenticated and service_role.
    * the acceptance surface: createProjectAsOperator, assignVolunteerAsOperator and the
      projectAssignment read-back in the contract, the fixture and the live adapter, plus the
      backed list.
    * tests/at/suites/req-001/_source-scan.ts - the executable oracle for AT-001.17's "UI absent"
      clause, shared by its loop and integration bodies. It reads the names under src/routes/ and
      the route paths in the generated route tree. Its residual is stated in the file: it is a
      NAMING oracle, so a deliberately renamed invite screen escapes it.
    * executable bodies for AT-001.17 and .32 at BOTH tiers, their declarations flipped green at
      both tiers, the D3.L2 label removed from the pending map (21 to 19), and the item's pending
      ledger listing the 19 that remain with the manifest leaf that will land each.
    
    The privilege posture on the new table is measured rather than asserted, which the plan gate
    required: after a reset on the item's own slot the catalog returns ZERO rows for the three
    Data API roles and has_table_privilege answers false for every probe, TRUNCATE and REFERENCES
    included. That measurement and its command are in the item record.
    
    Counts after both slices: loop 18 green / 19 red, integration 13 green / 24 red.
    
    The verify suite is deliberately NOT run in this pass.

